  "sport": "floorball",
  "title": "The M with a bonus – stay alert after the shot",
  "description": "A follow-on from the M. One line in each corner at one end and a cone on each side further out towards the middle. A runs down and round their cone, gets a diagonal pass from the first player in the other corner (D) and shoots first time. At the same time B starts their run on the other side.\n\nAfter the shot A turns back towards their own corner, gets the ball from the first player there (C) and plays it straight back. C then plays the diagonal pass to B, who has rounded their cone and shoots first time. Then B turns towards the other corner for their wall pass, and so it rolls on.\n\nIt is easy to switch off after a shot. Here the players learn to stay alert after it too. Rotation: after your wall pass, join the other line, so everyone shoots from both sides. The diagram is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "Do not switch off after the shot – turn towards your corner straight away."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "The first-time pass back should be firm and accurate."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "Play the diagonal pass early, in front of the runner."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp4",
      "text": "The runner shows with the stick where they want the ball."
    }
  ],
  "locale": "en",
